            <ArticleTitle>Managing asthma in Black children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>46-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000414596.39895.60</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Black children bear a disproportionate burden of asthma when compared to other segments of the population. This study assessed the role of symptom scores, spirometry testing, and serum-specific immunoglobulin E in the primary care management of asthma in Black children.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
